# Least Privilege Ticket Exercise — VDR

I chose these roles before checking Microsoft’s documentation.

| Task | My original choice | Reviewed choice |
|---|---|---|
| Reset a non-admin employee’s password | Password Administrator | Password Administrator |
| Create a new employee account | User Administrator | User Administrator |
| Create a Finance security group | Global Administrator | Groups Administrator |
| Assign User Administrator to Taylor | Privileged Role Administrator | Privileged Role Administrator |
| Read sign-in logs | Reports Reader | Reports Reader |
| Reset a Global Administrator’s password | Password Administrator | Privileged Authentication Administrator |

## What I learned

- Global Administrator grants more permissions than needed to create a group.
- Password reset permissions depend on the target user’s administrator role.
- Password Administrator cannot reset a Global Administrator’s password.
- Creating user accounts and assigning administrator roles require different permissions.

## Assumptions

The employee in the first ticket has no administrator role.
The Finance group is a normal security group, not a role-assignable group.
The administrator in the final ticket holds Global Administrator.

